 "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
 "applies_to": "Veris E50H2 and E50H5 DIN-rail power and energy meters with BACnet MS/TP; the E50H5 adds data logging and a real-time clock alert.",
 "summary": "The E50H2 and E50H5 are DIN-rail three-phase power meters with a BACnet MS/TP port. Measurements are Analog Inputs (energy, power, demand, volts, amps, power factor, frequency), setup is in eleven writable Analog Values (system type, CT and PT ratios, system voltage, demand intervals), and alerts are Binary Inputs that also roll up into AI 52. The E50H5 also has three Trend_Log objects.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The E50H5 adds Trend_Log objects TL1-TL3 (defaults: AI1, AI27, AI34; 5760 records, interval tied to AV 11). They have no names in the guide and are not listed as points.",
  "BI 15 RTC_Reset is present on the E50H5 only.",
  "AI 26 and AI 27 report kWh in their BACnet Units property because BACnet has no kVAh / kVARh unit.",
  "AV 1 Config always reads 0. Write 30078 to clear energy accumulators, 21211 to start a new demand sub-interval (sync-to-comms), 21212 to reset max demand, 16498 to clear pulse counters.",
  "BI 5 and BI 6 are printed with the name Current_Error_A; kept as printed. AI 40 / AI 41 use the E50H5 names (Pulse_Count_1 / _2); on the E50H2 AI 40 is Pulse Count and AI 41 is reserved."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "E50H2, E50H5 Compact Power and Energy Meters with BACnet MS/TP Support, Installation Guide",
